WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.936
-The crowded 2020 field
got another addition today

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.505
when Beto O'Rourke jumped in,

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.273
and President Trump
immediately attacked him.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.308
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:13.546
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.581
Trump and his advisers
are already putting together

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.483
his 2020 re-election campaign,

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.685
and they're not just staffing up
and raising money.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.787
They reportedly
want Trump's re-election bid

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:22.922
to be one of the biggest

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.058
and most sophisticated campaigns
in history.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.627
Trump's campaign manager told
"The Washington Post" this week,

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.729
"We are creating
the largest campaign operation

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.030
in American history.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.700
An unstoppable apparatus
that will follow and implement

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.067
President Trump's strategy."

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:38.238
An "unstoppable apparatus"?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.139
Are you talking about
your presidential campaign

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:42.575
or the Death Star?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:46.245
But, of course, Trump has to
create an unstoppable apparatus

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:48.214
because he's, perhaps,
the weakest candidate

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.049
of any sitting President
in recent history.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:52.952
Polls have shown that
a large majority of Americans

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.688
consider the President
both a criminal and a liar.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.424
And yesterday, the guy who ran
the President's last campaign,

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:01.193
Paul Manafort,
was both sentenced in one case

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.896
and indicted in another.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:05.831
Trump was asked by reporters
if he was considering a pardon

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.933
for Manafort,
and he insisted that he wasn't.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:09.502
-Will you pardon Paul Manafort?

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:13.339
-I have not even given it
a thought as of this moment.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.475
It's not something
that's right now on my mind.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.377
-Now, in fairness,
that's an accurate answer

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:20.446
to virtually any question
you could ask Donald Trump.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.448
[ Laughter ]
"Mr. President..."

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.883
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:27.387
For example, "Mr. President,
what is the role of government

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.621
in American life?"

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.123
"It's not something
that's on my mind."

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.224
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.558
Trump's brain
is capable of holding

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:34.093
exactly one thought at a time,

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:36.496
and it echoes through
his skull like a cave.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.264
-[ Echoing ] Hamburgers,
hamburgers.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.132
China, China, China.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:42.301
Golf, golf, golf.

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:44.503
-But the Russia investigation
and the various scandals

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:45.705
swirling around Trump

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.240
aren't the only things
making him vulnerable.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.208
In fact, this week,
he did something

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:51.610
that could potentially hurt him
more politically

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.079
than Robert Mueller ever could.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.980
He proposed a budget
that would gut

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.049
wildly popular
healthcare programs

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:59.385
that he specifically promised
he would never cut.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.221
-President Trump released
his budget for 2020 today,

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:05.190
proposing massive cuts to
government-funded healthcare.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:09.161
The President's budget
includes a cut of $845 billion

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:11.530
to Medicare
over the next 10 years

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.533
and $241 billion from Medicaid.

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:17.537
-So, Trump said he would
never cut Medicare or Medicaid,

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.506
and now he's cutting billions
from Medicare and Medicaid.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.808
Is there anything about this guy
that isn't a lie?

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:25.178
I'm starting to suspect
his fake hair

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.480
is covering a full head
of real hair.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.449
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:34.120
Trump's legal attacks and his
attacks on healthcare programs

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.055
have made him one of
the weakest incumbent presidents

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.558
in modern polling and left
a huge opening for Democrats,

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.659
which is why so many of them
are running for president.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.962
In the last few weeks,
Washington governor Jay Inslee

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.763
and former Colorado governor
John Hickenlooper

00:02:44.763 --> 00:02:46.132
have officially jumped in.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.434
Colorado Senator Michael Bennet
was in New Hampshire,

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.735
and New York City mayor
Bill de Blasio

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:50.903
was in South Carolina,

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:52.805
and Senator Elizabeth Warren
was in Queens,

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.107
and three more candidates
were in Texas

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:56.542
doing townhalls on CNN.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.078
In total, "The New York Times"
lists 15 candidates

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.279
who've already declared

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.047
and at least another eight
who might run.

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:03.783
Look at that.
There are so many people

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.551
on that screen,
you didn't even notice

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.119
that one of them was Carrot Top.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.088
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.491
And on top of all that,
"The New York Times" reported

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.559
that former Vice President
Joe Biden

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.728
is 95% committed to running,

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.431
and in this speech
to firefighters this week,

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.232
he teased --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:21.868
he teased a possible run.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:25.404
-You know,
I'd like you all to --

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:30.976
I appreciate the energy
you showed when I got up here.

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:32.278
Save it a little longer.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.980
I may need it in a few weeks.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.282
[ Cheers and applause ]
Be careful what you wish for.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.851
-No, dude,
be careful what you wish for.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.253
You really want to do this?

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.321
If you run for president,
everyone's gonna dig

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:44.523
through every dumb thing
you've said the last 40 years

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:45.691
and get mad at you.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.360
Why do you wanna
do that to yourself?

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.663
Right now, you're known
as Obama's wingman, Uncle Joe.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.698
The only guy who ever looked
like he was having fun

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.099
at the State of the Union.

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:55.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:58.103
I mean,
look at that party animal.

00:03:58.103 --> 00:03:59.872
He looks like
right after that was over,

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.008
he was gonna make Obama
do a keg stand.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.643
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:06.713
Then, there's former Texas
Senate candidate Beto O'Rourke,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.381
who officially jumped
into the race today

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.783
after spending weeks
teasing a possible run.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.686
Beto appears on the new cover
of "Vanity Fair" this week

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.354
with the headline
"Beto's Choice."

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:19.025
And, look, I'm a little upset it
took Beto this long to announce,

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.427
because if he'd done it in 2008,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:24.163
I definitely
could've played him on "SNL."

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.832
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.032
Definitely.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:29.535
I mean, it certainly was closer
than John Kerry.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.804
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:34.640
But the cover was not
the only eye-catching thing

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.041
about this profile.

00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:38.577
Beto also explained why
he wanted to run for president.

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.880
Now, it's a key question
for any candidate.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.649
People want to know
why you're doing this

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:43.982
and what you can bring
to the table.

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:46.318
It's a question
past candidates have flubbed,

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:48.153
and, in many cases,
it's doomed them.

00:04:48.153 --> 00:04:50.056
So, here's what Beto said.

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.792
"I think I'd be good at it.
I want to be in it.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.694
Man, I'm just born to be in it."

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:55.862
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.097
I'm sorry.
No one is born to be president.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.333
Nobody is born to be anything.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.135
Springsteen said
he was born to run,

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.237
and then he wrote
400 songs about New Jersey.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:05.605
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.773
I mean, look at Trump.
He wasn't born to be president.

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:08.907
If he was born to be anything,

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:11.410
it was selling fake Rolexes
in Times Square.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.179
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.948
Beto also talked
about his rise to fame,

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:18.517
the Senate campaign that
launched him to national stardom

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:21.187
and the very first event
he did in that campaign,

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.389
and his description
of that experience was --

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.623
Well, it was a little weird.

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:25.825
He told "Vanity Fair,"

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.927
"I honestly don't know
how much of it was me.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:30.129
But there is something abnormal.
Super normal.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:32.898
I got in there, and I don't know
if it's a speech or not,

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:34.634
but it felt amazing,
because every word

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:37.470
was pulled out of me,
like by some greater force

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.905
which was just the people there.

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.572
Everything that I said,
I was, like,

00:05:40.572 --> 00:05:43.509
watching myself being, like,
'How am I saying this stuff?

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.978
Where is this coming from?'"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:49.682
Now, in the run-up to 2020,
we here at "Late Night,"

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.750
we're gonna try really hard,
and we're gonna ask yourselves,

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:55.487
"Would we make fun of
Donald Trump if he said that?"

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:57.890
So, let's see.
"Because every word

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.760
was pulled out of me, like,
by some greater force,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.128
which was just the people there.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.796
Everything that I said,
I was, like,

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.632
watching myself being, like,
'How am I saying this stuff?

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.933
Where is it coming from?'"

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.968
Yeah, no, Beto,
that was [bleep] weird, yeah.

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:11.070
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.505
That was a [bleep]
weird thing to say.

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:18.677
Seriously. I did not know
that weed was legal in Texas.

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:21.247
And when Beto went to Iowa today
for his first official event

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.548
since announcing his campaign,

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.049
there were
a few more weird moments.

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:25.518
For example,
at the end of his speech,

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:27.953
a lady in the crowd forced him
to make it absolutely clear

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:29.589
that he was
running for president.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:30.756
-Thank you.

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:33.792
I cannot tell you
how much this means to me.

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.728
I will remember this forever --

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:37.930
every single one of your faces
and what you were wearing,

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.865
what you had to drink.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:41.600
-Let us remember it!

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.903
Tell us
that you're going to run.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:46.872
Announce it now for us.
-He already did.

00:06:46.872 --> 00:06:48.140
-I'm running to serve you

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.042
as President of
the United States of America.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.376
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:51.376 --> 00:06:54.046
-Man, I don't know who
that lady is, but I love her.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:55.280
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:57.783
She should moderate
every presidential debate.

00:06:57.783 --> 00:07:00.352
"You have five seconds.
Now spit it out!"

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:02.354
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:02.354 --> 00:07:05.824
And yet as weird as Beto's
launch has been so far,

00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:08.160
as always, Trump and his allies
on Fox News

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.895
have found a way
to outweird him.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.664
For example,
the "Vanity Fair" profile

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:13.766
mentions some of the books
Beto has in his house,

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:17.136
and Fox News host Brian Kilmeade
was apparently baffled by that.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:19.772
-"Vanity Fair" has a huge
article and feature on him.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:22.541
It's almost as if they helped
launch his campaign.

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:23.976
Here's a quote from it.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.478
He says,
"I want to be in it, man.

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:27.012
I'm just born to be in it."

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:29.882
They also point out
that he has this huge library,

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:32.318
as if it's a big plus
that he reads books.

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:36.388
-I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:38.657
It is a plus.

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:40.292
Reading is definitely...

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:41.960
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:46.065
It's definitely a plus
for a president.

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:48.467
Also, just so you know,
when you attack someone

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.269
for reading books,

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.837
you're really
attacking yourself.

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:53.105
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.241
Although I'm not surprised
Kilmeade is anti-book.

00:07:55.241 --> 00:07:56.775
I bet if you open one
in his house,

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:58.477
there would just be
a hollowed-out spot

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:00.312
for a Snickers.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.312 --> 00:08:01.847
"I see you found 'Moby Dick.'

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:03.749
I think you'll find
it's delicious."

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:04.917
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:06.651
And Fox News is not
the only cable channel

00:08:06.651 --> 00:08:08.988
that's taken a keen interest
in Beto's announcement.

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:11.657
There was also MSNBC,
which honed in on even

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:13.526
the smallest details
of Beto's trip to Iowa.

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:15.627
For example,
they seemed especially fixated

00:08:15.627 --> 00:08:17.062
on his minivan.

00:08:17.062 --> 00:08:19.965
-Beto O'Rourke is driving
himself in his Dodge Caravan.

00:08:19.965 --> 00:08:21.299
-Where is he?

00:08:21.299 --> 00:08:24.170
-And he's arriving here
to Fort Madison High School.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.672
-Yvonne, do we know
how the minivan got to Iowa,

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:29.608
if it's a rental
that he acquired there

00:08:29.608 --> 00:08:32.912
or if this is sort of
the O'Rourke family minivan

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:36.615
that has now been moved to Iowa
for campaign purposes?

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:39.151
-It looks like an Illinois van.

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:42.421
This is about three hours away
from any major city.

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:46.124
The question, Congressman,
is where is the rental car from?

00:08:46.124 --> 00:08:47.359
-Des Moines.
-Des Moines.

00:08:47.359 --> 00:08:48.761
-Picked it up
in the Des Moines airport.

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:50.496
-Wow.
Hard-hitting stuff, you guys.

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:51.930
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.367
"Did you use Hertz or Avis?!
Answer the question!"

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:55.467
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.636
"Will you release
your minivan returns?!"

00:08:57.636 --> 00:09:00.005
[ Laughter ]
Then there was Trump.

00:09:00.005 --> 00:09:02.742
Today, Trump is dealing with
an urgent airline-safety issue,

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:04.009
a resolution from the House

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:05.744
calling for the Mueller report
to be made public,

00:09:05.744 --> 00:09:07.946
an unprecedented rebuke
from the Senate

00:09:07.946 --> 00:09:09.915
over his national emergency
declaration,

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:11.751
and dozens of scandals
and investigations

00:09:11.751 --> 00:09:12.985
of every aspect of his life,

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:14.520
not to mention he was meeting

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.955
with the prime minister
of Ireland.

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:19.658
But amid all of that, he just
had to take a swipe at Beto.

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:21.159
-What's your reaction
to Beto O'Rourke's announcement

00:09:21.159 --> 00:09:22.428
today, Mr. President?

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:23.729
-Well, I think he's got
a lot of hand movement.

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.397
I've never seen
so much hand movement.

00:09:25.397 --> 00:09:28.634
I said, "Is he crazy or is
that just the way he acts?

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:29.802
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:33.172
-I'm sorry,
are you accusing someone else

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:36.075
of having weird hand movements
and acting crazy?

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:37.876
Every time
you do a press conference,

00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:40.046
you look like you're playing
an invisible accordion.

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:41.814
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:44.115
"You guys ready
for the liars polka?"

00:09:44.115 --> 00:09:46.852
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:49.588
Now, Beto is jumping into
a crowded field

00:09:49.588 --> 00:09:51.524
that already has several
established candidates

00:09:51.524 --> 00:09:53.058
who have spent weeks
laying the groundwork

00:09:53.058 --> 00:09:54.359
in early primary states,

00:09:54.359 --> 00:09:56.361
like Bernie Sanders,
who was in Iowa last week.

00:09:56.361 --> 00:09:58.564
And when he mentioned
climate change, this happened.

00:09:58.564 --> 00:10:04.136
-Tonight, we say to Donald Trump
and the fossil-fuel industry...

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:06.505
[ Crowd booing ]
-[Bleep]

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:09.608
[ Laughter ]

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:12.878
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:12.878 --> 00:10:15.481
-Well...

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:18.284
That is
one way of phrasing it.

00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:19.585
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.585 --> 00:10:21.987
I, myself, was gonna say it
a little bit differently.

00:10:21.987 --> 00:10:23.222
I am a senator, you know.

00:10:23.222 --> 00:10:25.657
-Man, you could just tell
from his face

00:10:25.657 --> 00:10:27.026
that he wanted to say it.

00:10:27.026 --> 00:10:28.260
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.861
And it would make things
a lot more entertaining

00:10:29.861 --> 00:10:31.429
if Bernie
was just totally unleashed.

00:10:31.429 --> 00:10:32.832
Can you imagine
how much bleeping

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:34.332
they'd have to do on C-SPAN?

00:10:34.332 --> 00:10:37.369
-Donald Trump
is a [bleep]...

00:10:37.369 --> 00:10:39.772
[ Laughter ]

00:10:39.772 --> 00:10:42.174
...and a [bleep]

00:10:42.174 --> 00:10:44.610
-Now, some of these candidates
are more well known than others,

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.611
but one lesser-known candidate
who seems to be gaining

00:10:46.611 --> 00:10:49.114
a lot of traction this week
is Pete Buttigieg,

00:10:49.114 --> 00:10:50.849
the mayor of South Bend,
Indiana.

00:10:50.849 --> 00:10:53.485
Buttigieg got rave reviews
for his performance

00:10:53.485 --> 00:10:55.821
at a townhall on CNN on Sunday
where he said this

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:57.256
about Vice President Mike Pence,

00:10:57.256 --> 00:10:59.091
who was previously
the governor of Indiana.

00:10:59.091 --> 00:11:02.995
-How could he allow himself
to become the cheerleader

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:04.796
of the porn-star presidency?

00:11:04.796 --> 00:11:06.431
-And that is
such a great analogy,

00:11:06.431 --> 00:11:08.701
because this presidency
is definitely like a porno.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:11.237
And Pence might be able to tell
himself he's not the star,

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:12.537
he's not the one having sex,

00:11:12.537 --> 00:11:13.973
he didn't take his clothes off,

00:11:13.973 --> 00:11:16.675
but he's definitely the guy
watching through the keyhole.

00:11:16.675 --> 00:11:18.077
[ Laughter ]

00:11:18.077 --> 00:11:19.978
Democrats are eager
to take on Trump

00:11:19.978 --> 00:11:21.713
because he's
the weakest incumbent President

00:11:21.713 --> 00:11:24.049
in recent history --
he's beset by scandals,

00:11:24.049 --> 00:11:26.085
and he's gutting Medicare,
and on top of that,

00:11:26.085 --> 00:11:28.587
voters are looking at Trump
and asking themselves...

00:11:28.587 --> 00:11:31.090
-Is he crazy or is that
just the way he acts?

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.758
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:11:32.758 --> 00:11:36.429
[ Cheers and applause ]

